Follow-up to live r514 (PR #495, merge a280b828). Person prosrc was `eb02f76ec94cd0b6c824a18660432afa`. Mark prosrc stays `f5bdb212b439fd37adb73860c5e5d4d3`.

## Numbering

Live `pdc_ops.regression_checks` already has r512 / F125 / sort 297, r513 / F126 / sort 300, and r514 / F128 / sort 301. Open PRs #493 and #496 both claim r512. #496 also claims F128, which r514 already owns. This release is r515 / F129 / sort 302.

## What changed

`record_pdc_person_parts_complete_20260913` only. `outlook_ok` still requires mailbox and To `pdc@pmgwa.com.au`, `verified_by` `microsoft_receiving_provider`, an id of length 8–512 with no whitespace that equals `internet_message_id` or `outlook_message_id` or `microsoft_message_id`, and an Authentication-Results value that starts with `mx.microsoft.com`.

Then either:

- the r514 external path: DKIM, DMARC or SPF pass for the sender domain, or
- the internal path: `auth_as` or `x_ms_exchange_organization_authas` is `Internal`, the sender domain is `pmgwa.com.au`, and the copied Authentication-Results contains `header.from=pmgwa.com.au`.

`auth_source` and `x_ms_exchange_organization_authsource` are optional. Leave both out when the message has no AuthSource header. Do not invent one. If a key is present, the value must be one hostname (letters, digits, dots, hyphens, 1–253 characters, no spaces). If both keys are present they must be the same hostname, ignoring case. A blank value fails.

The Gmail branch is the r514 text. `mark_pdc_parts_complete` is not replaced. Karratha confirmation CHECKs are not replaced. `service_role` is not granted EXECUTE. Pin count stays 225. These two functions are not in `expected_function_md5`.

A null `authentication_results` now fails closed. r514 could leave `outlook_ok` null and fall through.

## Evidence

Do not rewrite this Authentication-Results. It is the header on the message that failed:

`mx.microsoft.com 1; dkim=none (message not signed) header.d=none;dmarc=none action=none header.from=pmgwa.com.au;`

`X-MS-Exchange-Organization-AuthAs: Internal`

internetMessageId `<SY1P282MB63556EA203EA75E467DCAC23AC642@SY1P282MB6355.AUSP282.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM>`
mailbox `pdc@pmgwa.com.au`
from `talin.parker@pmgwa.com.au`
evidence_sha256 `c94f7ca4357c95113dbfcb15cd93cb21d24d9714ad99056cbaaf59bfcdda8656`

AuthSource was not supplied for this message. Omit `auth_source`.

## jsonb Kajel passes

`p_gmail_message_id` is the historical parameter name. Pass the internetMessageId there, including the angle brackets. Stock, subject and body rules are unchanged from r514 (body `Parts complete` is enough on the Outlook path when the subject contains the stock).

```json
{
  "mailbox": "pdc@pmgwa.com.au",
  "to_address": "pdc@pmgwa.com.au",
  "from_address": "talin.parker@pmgwa.com.au",
  "header_from": "pmgwa.com.au",
  "verified_by": "microsoft_receiving_provider",
  "internet_message_id": "<SY1P282MB63556EA203EA75E467DCAC23AC642@SY1P282MB6355.AUSP282.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM>",
  "authentication_results": "mx.microsoft.com 1; dkim=none (message not signed) header.d=none;dmarc=none action=none header.from=pmgwa.com.au;",
  "auth_as": "Internal",
  "human_message": "true",
  "unquoted_affirmative": "true",
  "auto_submitted": "no"
}
```

`header_from` is the sender domain in lowercase. It must equal the domain of `from_address`. `human_message` and `unquoted_affirmative` are the strings `true`. Omit `reply_to`, or set it to the same address as `from_address`.

Accepted AuthAs keys, value `Internal` (trim and case ignored). If both are sent they must agree:

- `auth_as`
- `x_ms_exchange_organization_authas` (the header `X-MS-Exchange-Organization-AuthAs`)

Optional AuthSource keys. Omit both for this message:

- `auth_source`
- `x_ms_exchange_organization_authsource` (the header `X-MS-Exchange-Organization-AuthSource`)

Copy `authentication_results` as received. Do not add `spf=pass`, `dkim=pass` or `dmarc=pass`.

